# The Living Map artifact is GENERATED (docs/prototypes/gen_*.py, embed_*.py)
# and is ~4 MB of HTML with base64 payloads inlined. `core.autocrlf` is true on
# Windows checkouts, so without this git would store LF, hand back CRLF, and
# the file on disk would no longer match the one the generator wrote or the one
# the map lane checksums. `-text` means bytes in, same bytes out, everywhere.
docs/prototypes/grounds-v0.html -text

# docs/TOKENS.md is GENERATED (scripts/generate-token-doc.mjs) and a build step
# compares the committed bytes with what the generator writes. `core.autocrlf`
# is true on the Windows checkouts this repo is developed on, so without this
# git would store LF, hand back CRLF, and the guard would fail on one machine
# and pass in CI. `-text` means bytes in, same bytes out, everywhere. The guard
# strips carriage returns as well, so a hand edit in an editor that writes CRLF
# still reads as content rather than as a whole-file difference.
docs/TOKENS.md -text

# docs/GOVERNANCE.md is GENERATED (scripts/generate-governance-doc.mjs) and
# guarded the same way its sibling above is, so it needs the same byte pinning
# for the same reason.
docs/GOVERNANCE.md -text

# docs/VARIABLES.md, docs/MODULES.md and docs/CAPABILITIES.md are GENERATED
# (scripts/generate-*-doc.mjs) and each has a CI guard that regenerates and
# compares. Same reason as docs/TOKENS.md above: `core.autocrlf` is true on the
# Windows checkouts this repo is developed on, so without `-text` git would
# store LF, hand back CRLF, and the guards would fail on one machine while
# passing in CI. Bytes in, same bytes out, everywhere.
docs/VARIABLES.md -text
docs/MODULES.md -text
docs/CAPABILITIES.md -text

# What `git archive` leaves out. GitHub builds every release's "Source code"
# downloads with it, and the release workflow builds the starter kit with it.
# The maintainers' internal notes moved to a private repository on 2026-10-02
# and scripts/check-public-tree.mjs refuses them in the tree; these lines keep
# any copy that slips past both out of a published archive as well.
SEASON2_FLEET_LEDGER.md export-ignore
CLAUDE_CODE_PROMPT_* export-ignore
FIXES_TO_MAKE_* export-ignore
SESSION_HANDOFF.md export-ignore
PLAN_TO_A.md export-ignore
.env export-ignore
.env.* export-ignore
# Attributes have no negation, so the template is switched back on by name.
.env.example -export-ignore
